A node that is neither a string nor a mapping fails the run, and the error addresses it by
its full dotted path through the tree, not by the tree's root.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  e2e_demo:
    tree:
      one:
        two: null
-- cmd --
booping scaffold core.e2e_demo.tree out
-- exit --
1
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
error: core.e2e_demo.tree.one.two: node is null — use "" for an empty file or {} for an empty dir
